WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.863
- All right, it's been a super fun,

00:00:01.863 --> 00:00:03.229
sometimes frightening hour.

00:00:03.229 --> 00:00:04.890
But let's close out
with some Halloween joy.

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.002
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:06.002 --> 00:00:08.015
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.015 --> 00:00:08.940
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.400
All right, so dressing up and
going door to door for candy

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.902
is a childhood rite of passage.

00:00:12.902 --> 00:00:14.970
A Houston high schooler wants to make sure

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:16.650
that every kid gets that opportunity,

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.390
no matter their financial means.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.150
So he created Y'allowen, which I love.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.070
He distributes brand-new costumes

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:24.930
to kids in need in his community.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.340
And we have him on the line right now,

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:27.390
along with his mama.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:29.130
Say hi to BJ and Tracy

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.979
watching on Fox 26, everybody. (clapping)

00:00:30.979 --> 00:00:33.352
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:33.352 --> 00:00:34.765
What's up, y'all?

00:00:34.765 --> 00:00:36.065
- Hi, Kelly.
- Hi, Kelly.

00:00:36.065 --> 00:00:37.215
- Oh my God, love.

00:00:37.215 --> 00:00:38.730
This is the coolest thing ever

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.080
'cause, by the way, I
was one of those kids

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.240
that totally could've
used money for costume.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.370
So how did this start?

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:46.080
- It started back three years ago

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.820
when we started the Pandemic.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.740
We saw that there was a lot
of people who lost their jobs

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:52.080
and that kids weren't
able to get costumes.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.370
So, I just love Halloween.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.840
I cannot go without it.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.226
And so we really wanted to spread that.

00:00:56.226 --> 00:00:57.690
And so we became Y'allowen,

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.229
which is Halloween for all y'all.

00:01:00.229 --> 00:01:01.505
- Aw, I love it.

00:01:01.505 --> 00:01:03.780
(gasps) Mama, great job.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.000
What a beautiful young man, your heart.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.700
So, how many costumes do y'all do a year?

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.830
- So, since our first year in 2021,

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:13.782
we've distributed over 750 costumes.

00:01:13.782 --> 00:01:14.745
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:01:14.745 --> 00:01:17.610
- The way it works is we
have partner organizations

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.770
that support transitional housing

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.080
or domestic violence abuse victims.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.930
And they give us a list of
the kids in their programs

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:26.880
with their gender and their age,

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.820
and if they wanna be a
princess or a superhero,

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:31.440
and then we match 'em up with costumes

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:32.730
that have been donated

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:36.030
or that BJ has raised money
to buy for his fundraising.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.010
I am so incredibly proud of BJ.

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:40.710
My kids have never wanted for anything,

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:41.970
and he's helping these parents

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.830
that are having tough economic times

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.660
provide a little bit of normality

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.280
and some joy to these kids

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.200
on our favorite holiday, Halloween.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.670
- Absolutely, it's escapism.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.650
Every kid, you know, should get that joy

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.240
of like the theme of dressing
up whatever you want.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.490
And being creative,
there's so much into it.

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:59.010
My kids love it, specifically my son.

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.630
Thank you so much, BJ,

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:01.650
for just having such a great heart,

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:02.700
and Tracy, thank you so much

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.780
for raising such a great young man.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.610
I'm liking your post right now, all right?

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.230
- Thank you so much, Kelly.
- Yeah.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:08.190
And that's not all, guys.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:09.750
Our season-long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:10.650
makers of FriXion,

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.990
the go-to erasable pen of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.970
recognize that you're giving
kids in your community

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.500
the gift of a simple pleasure.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.510
So they're giving you a thousand dollars

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.070
to get started on your efforts for

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:21.471
next year's costumes.
- Oh my God.

00:02:21.471 --> 00:02:22.304
- Thank you so much.

00:02:22.304 --> 00:02:24.820
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:26.653
- Thank you guys so much!

00:02:26.653 --> 00:02:28.320
Making Texas proud!

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.940
And thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.640
Kyle Richards, Keith
Morrison, DC Young Fly,

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.513
Rick, Kate, and Simona.

00:02:34.513 --> 00:02:36.210
Y'all have a great Halloween.

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:37.043
If it's not, try and change it.

00:02:37.043 --> 00:02:37.876
(audience clapping)

